        "objective": "In its own research branch, modify only src/candidate.cpp to test scalar scheduling improvements to the existing table-driven eight-character/six-byte decode loop: unroll multiple independent groups so table lookups can overlap and loop overhead is amortized. Keep this a scalar-focused contrast to the SIMD trees; do not add explicit SIMD or parallel execution. Preserve exact output semantics, safe tails/padding, and the threads budget. Validate empty and short strings, lengths around the unrolled-group boundary, every padding case, random valid inputs, and the official Lena input before repeated native timing. Do not specialize to the benchmark length; record unsuccessful unroll/group-size choices and results.",
